-- A call script for examples/lists.lang (kit slice K4c): cons writes and nil on a List field, and folds over it.
-- nil on the empty List, then three cons writes (one word, two words, one word). The view paidSum is the sum;
-- the view weighted folds the elements as a base-2 polynomial from the last element to the head; settle writes the sum to tally.
-- settleWith 5u writes 5 plus the sum to tally (a fold over cons 5u on the field); paidSum shows the List did not change.
-- The view over is the max word at tally 0 (now 99) and traps at tally 25 (now 113): a view that traps (O-c4-3).
99 99u 0x00000000000000000000000000000000000000bb over
100 100u 0x00000000000000000000000000000000000000bb wipe
101 101u 0x00000000000000000000000000000000000000bb paidSum
102 102u 0x00000000000000000000000000000000000000bb pushOne 7u
103 103u 0x00000000000000000000000000000000000000bb paidSum
104 104u 0x00000000000000000000000000000000000000bb pushTwo 9u
105 105u 0x00000000000000000000000000000000000000bb paidSum
106 106u 0x00000000000000000000000000000000000000bb weighted
107 107u 0x00000000000000000000000000000000000000bb pushOne 3u
108 108u 0x00000000000000000000000000000000000000bb paidSum
109 109u 0x00000000000000000000000000000000000000bb weighted
110 110u 0x00000000000000000000000000000000000000bb settle
111 111u 0x00000000000000000000000000000000000000bb settleWith 5u
112 112u 0x00000000000000000000000000000000000000bb paidSum
113 113u 0x00000000000000000000000000000000000000bb over
